// data_views.h: names of the original's globals that lie INSIDE a bigger object (an overlap: g_keyboard, g_options, g_cfg, g_render,
// g_bit, g_skill_tbl, g_dialogs ...). A name that is its own variable next to the object is a second storage for the same bytes: the code
// that fills one never sees the other (D2's g_screen_w left the viewport at 0x0). Here each such name is a view of the outer object's
// bytes: the outer object's label (g_ovl_<address>, bound to the object by its address) plus the offset. Generated by ovl_fix.py;
// replace a view by a real member of the outer type when it gets one.
